  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">OEGI- Western Kenya Water Activity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Kenya):  Using FY 2022 funds, USAID will continue its support for the Western Kenya Water activity that partners with eight counties and the private sector in Kenya to ensure county-wide sustainable drinking water services to households and to improve the management of water resources. .The activity will professionalize rural water services and strengthen water utilities while protecting watersheds and effectively managing the water resources.  In urban areas served by utilities and water and sanitation companies (WASCOs), the activity will partner with the private sector, government, and civil society to improve the quality of services, monitor service delivery, and enforce environmental standards..The activity will also strengthen counties&apos; institutional capacity to plan, finance, and manage water services, enabling county governments to provide reliable water service for its citizens.  Finally, the activity will allow financial institutions to offer commercial loans to emerging water companies and create partnerships in the water sector. This approach will foster stable, resilient, self-reliant, and prosperous counties, and directly contribute to the U.S. Global Water Strategy of providing sustainable access to water and sanitation in Kenya. This helps reduce conflict over resources, contributing to regional stability, another U.S. Foreign Policy priority.The protection of watersheds and effective management of water resources strengthens hydromet data collection, county level early warning systems, and drought management systems. This enhances access and preparedness to the changing climate context. This activity supports  the 2022-2027 USAID Biodiversity Policy and Climate Strategy.. ...</narrative>
  </description>
